;;; ====================================================================
;;; theorem-library/product-measure.scm -- PRODUCT SIGMA-ALGEBRAS, SECTIONS,
;;; DYNKIN'S PI-LAMBDA THEOREM, and FUBINI'S THEOREM for non-negative functions.
;;; Agent FUBINI-1, 2026-10-10 (scratchpad/triage/FUBINI-1.md).  Library: measure.
;;; Helper prefix pms-.  Vocabulary: structure-library/product-measure.scm.
;;; 81 theorems, every one `modulo 0'; no support, warrant!, stamp or add-axiom!.
;;;
;;; SOURCE.  Thayer, Construction of Measures, Ch. 3 s.2 (pp. 22-23): the product
;;; sigma-algebra A (x) B, Prop. 3.5, Def. 3.6 (IS-SIGMA-FINITE), Thm. 3.7 (Fubini),
;;; Def. 3.8 (the product measure).
;;;
;;; THE THEOREMS THE NOTES STATE:
;;;   x-section-measurable / y-section-measurable   C in A (x) B, x in X  ==>  C_x in B
;;;                                                 (and the mirror)
;;;   fn-x-section-measurable / fn-y-...            PROP. 3.5: f A (x) B measurable  ==>
;;;                                                 y |-> f(x, y) B measurable (and mirror)
;;;   fubini-sets                                   Thm. 3.7 for indicators: mu, nu
;;;                                                 sigma-finite, C in A (x) B  ==>  x |-> nu(C_x),
;;;                                                 y |-> mu(C^y) measurable, equal integrals
;;;   fubini                                        THM. 3.7: mu, nu sigma-finite, f >= 0
;;;                                                 A (x) B measurable  ==>  both inner
;;;                                                 integrals measurable, iterated integrals equal
;;;   product-measure-is-measure                    DEF. 3.8: mu, nu sigma-finite  ==>
;;;                                                 rho = PRODUCT-MEASURE is a measure on A (x) B
;;;   product-measure-symmetric                     rho(C) = integral over Y of mu(C^y) d nu
;;;   product-measure-rectangle                     rho(aa x bb) = mu(aa) nu(bb), FINITE sides
;;;                                                 (infinite sides are not proved: that needs
;;;                                                 sup_n etimes(a_n, b_n) = etimes(sup a_n, sup b_n)
;;;                                                 for nondecreasing a_n, b_n in [0, inf])
;;; AND THE GENERAL FACTS ON THE WAY (each usable on its own):
;;;   dynkin-pi-lambda             a Dynkin system containing a pi-system contains the
;;;                                sigma-algebra it generates (with dynkin-generated-*,
;;;                                dynkin-inter-section, dynkin-pi-is-sigma-algebra)
;;;   rectangles-pi-system, product-sigma-is-sigma-algebra, rectangle-in-product-sigma
;;;   integral-finsum              the integral of a finite sum of measurable functions
;;;                                is the finite sum of the integrals
;;;   integral-esum                Beppo Levi: the integral of a series of non-negative
;;;                                measurable functions is the series of the integrals
;;;   esum-as-esup-prefix          ESUM(f) is the supremum of the prefix sums
;;;   integral-congruence-ptwise, measurable-fn-congruence-ptwise, (measurable-fn-scale: removed at integration, = ptwise-scale-measurable)
;;;   measure-union-finite, measure-seg-union-finite, sigma-finite-increasing
;;;                                (a sigma-finite measure has a NONDECREASING exhaustion)
;;;   fubini-set-rectangle, fubini-set-difference, fubini-set-union,
;;;   fubini-set-in-finite-rectangle, fubini-simple, x-/y-section-integral-limit
;;;   plumbing: cartesian-membership-nth, pair-cartesian-iff, cartesian-in-power-product,
;;;   cartesian-intersection, cartesian-mono, the section membership / unfold / mono /
;;;   difference / rectangle / empty laws, the apply and typing laws of the section
;;;   functions and of the product measure (product-measure-apply).
;;;
;;; THE ROUTE (where it is not the notes').
;;;   * The notes reach A (x) B through the MONOTONE CLASS theorem over the algebra of
;;;     finite (disjoint) unions of rectangles.  That algebra is never built here: the
;;;     rectangles are a PI-SYSTEM (one set identity, cartesian-intersection), and
;;;     Dynkin's pi-lambda theorem (proved here, 7 theorems, on the model of
;;;     monotone-class.scm) puts A (x) B inside any Dynkin system containing them.  The
;;;     Fubini class is checked to be a Dynkin system: proper differences by
;;;     integral-sub (finiteness needed), nondecreasing unions by monotone convergence.
;;;   * Sections of SETS need no monotone class: the C with measurable sections form a
;;;     sigma-algebra containing the rectangles.  Prop. 3.5 then goes by LEVEL SETS:
;;;     { y : alpha < f(x, y) } is the section at x of { w : alpha < f(w) }, so no
;;;     approximation by step functions is needed (the brief's preferred route).
;;;   * Thm. 3.7: indicators of C cut down to a rectangle B x D of finite measure first
;;;     (fubini-set-in-finite-rectangle, the Dynkin argument); a sigma-finite measure has
;;;     a nondecreasing exhaustion (sigma-finite-increasing), the cuts C n (B_n x D_n)
;;;     increase to C, and fubini-set-union closes the set case (fubini-sets).  No
;;;     restricted measure is ever formed.  Simple functions: the inner integral of a
;;;     simple s is  sum over v in s(X x Y) of v nu(section of {s = v})  (simple-integral-
;;;     partition), so integral-finsum and the set case give both iterated integrals as
;;;     sum_v v (integral of the section measure of {s = v}) (fubini-simple).  General f:
;;;     integral-simple-approx and monotone convergence, inside and outside.
;;;   * Def. 3.8: countable additivity of rho is nu's additivity on the (disjoint) sections
;;;     and integral-esum (proved here from integral-finsum on the prefixes and monotone
;;;     convergence on their supremum).
;;;
;;; REPRESENTATION.  A point of X x Y is the pair (LIST x y); a function on X x Y is
;;; applied to the pair, f((LIST x y)), never f(x, y) (FN-X-SECTION, FN-Y-SECTION).
;;;
;;; LOAD WINDOW: after "theorem-library/monotone-class" (load.scm 3490:
;;; algebra-monotone-union-sigma-algebra); integral-convergence (3477: monotone-
;;; convergence, integral-additive, integral-sub, integral-simple-approx,
;;; measurable-fn-sub / -const / -eplus / -eplus-of-values / -etimes-of-values,
;;; simple-fn-of-partition), integral-laws (3387), measure-laws (3386),
;;; structure-library/outer-measure-construction (3482: IS-SIGMA-FINITE), rake-measure
;;; and earlier files.  Slots: "structure-library/product-measure" then this file,
;;; after "theorem-library/monotone-class".  libraries.sexp: both in library measure.
;;; No top-level macro: the file may be compiled.
;;; ====================================================================

