(gloss! 'dynkin-pi-lambda
  "Dynkin's pi-lambda theorem: a Dynkin system over X (X in it, closed under proper
   differences and nondecreasing countable unions) that contains a family closed under
   binary intersection contains the sigma-algebra the family generates.")
(gloss! 'x-section-measurable
  "Thayer, Construction of Measures, Ch. 3 s.2: the section C_x = { y : (x, y) in C } of a
   set C of the product sigma-algebra A (x) B is in B.")
(gloss! 'fn-x-section-measurable
  "Thayer, Construction of Measures, Prop. 3.5 (p. 22): if f : X x Y -> [0, inf] is
   A (x) B measurable, then y |-> f(x, y) is B measurable for each x in X.")
(gloss! 'fubini-sets
  "Thayer, Construction of Measures, Thm. 3.7 for indicator functions: for sigma-finite
   mu, nu and C in A (x) B, x |-> nu(C_x) and y |-> mu(C^y) are measurable and their
   integrals agree.")
(gloss! 'integral-finsum
  "The integral of a finite sum of non-negative measurable functions is the sum of their
   integrals, and the sum is measurable.")
(gloss! 'fubini
  "Thayer, Construction of Measures, Thm. 3.7 (Fubini, p. 22): for sigma-finite measure
   spaces (X, A, mu), (Y, B, nu) and a non-negative A (x) B measurable f, the functions
   x |-> integral over Y of f(x, y) d nu(y) and y |-> integral over X of f(x, y) d mu(x)
   are measurable and the two iterated integrals agree.")
(gloss! 'integral-esum
  "Beppo Levi: the integral of the pointwise sum of a series of non-negative measurable
   functions is the sum of their integrals, and the sum is measurable.")
(gloss! 'product-measure-is-measure
  "Thayer, Construction of Measures, Def. 3.8 (p. 23): for sigma-finite (X, A, mu) and
   (Y, B, nu), rho(C) = integral over X of nu(C_x) d mu(x) is a countably additive measure
   on the product sigma-algebra A (x) B.")
